UnitDynamicSwapFeeHook::_GetFirstSwapFee
├── when base fee is ZERO_FEE_INDICATOR
│   └── it should return (0, ZERO_FEE_INDICATOR)
└── when base fee is not zero fee indicator
    ├── when observe call reverts
    │   └── it should return (base fee, bas fee)
    ├── when initial fee is enabled
    │   ├── when initial fee override is 0
    │   │   └── it should return (base fee, total fee)
    │   ├── when initial fee override is ZERO_FEE_INDICATOR
    │   │   └── it should return (0, total fee)
    │   └── when initial fee override is non zero
    │       └── it should return (initial fee, total fee)
    └── when initial fee is not enabled
        ├── when scaling factor is not set on the pool
        │   ├── when observation cardinality is insufficient
        │   │   ├── when discount is zero
        │   │   │   └── it should return (baseFee, baseFee)
        │   │   └── when discount is gt zero
        │   │       └── it should return (discounted base fee, base fee)
        │   └── when observation cardinality is sufficient
        │       ├── when observations latest slot is uninitialized
        │       │   ├── when latest observation timestamp is lt seconds ago
        │       │   │   └── it should fall back to observations(0) and return base fee
        │       │   └── when latest observation timestamp is geq seconds ago
        │       │       └── it should fall back to observations(0) and return base fee with dynamic fee
        │       ├── when total fee is lt fee cap
        │       │   ├── when discount is zero_
        │       │   │   └── it should return (total fee, total fee)
        │       │   └── when discount is gt zero_
        │       │       └── it should return (discounted total fee, total fee)
        │       └── when total fee is gt fee cap
        │           ├── when discount is zero__
        │           │   └── it should return (fee cap, fee cap)
        │           └── when discount is gt zero__
        │               └── it should return (discounted fee cap, fee cap)
        └── when scaling factor is set on the pool
            └── when observation cardinality is sufficient_
                ├── when observations latest slot is uninitialized_
                │   ├── when latest observation timestamp is lt seconds ago_
                │   │   └── it should fall back to observations(0) and return base fee
                │   └── when latest observation timestamp is geq seconds ago_
                │       └── it should fall back to observations(0) and return base fee with dynamic fee
                ├── when total fee is lt fee cap_
                │   ├── when discount is zero___
                │   │   └── it should return (total fee, total fee)
                │   └── when discount is gt zero___
                │       └── it should return (discounted total fee, total fee)
                └── when total fee is gt fee cap_
                    ├── when discount is zero____
                    │   └── it should return (fee cap, fee cap)
                    └── when discount is gt zero____
                        └── it should return (discounted fee cap, fee cap)
